{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1559555-obscure-1e-question-who-wrote-the-letter-in-baptism-by-fire","id":1559555,"title":"Obscure 1E question: Who wrote the letter in 'Baptism by Fire'?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-04-21T20:22:01-07:00","id":1559555,"title":"Obscure 1E question: Who wrote the letter in 'Baptism by Fire'?","content":"I am using Vampire 20th Edition to run the players through the original Chicago Chronicle from 1E. After spending a number of sessions with the players getting themselves situated in Gary, we have kicked off 'Ashes to Ashes'.<br /> <br /> Note - this post contains major spoilers for 'Ashes to Ashes' and the other Chicago Chronicle books. They're 35 years old, but hey, I'm running them, maybe your GM might want to as well, so warning given!<br /> <br /> I am mapping out 'Ashes to Ashes', just to make sure I understand what's really going on, and there is one major question I know my players are going to ask. For the life of me, I cannot find the answer - so I figured if anyone is likely to know, maybe it is someone here!<br /> <br /> Ok, so, what is really going on in this scenario:<br /> <br /> As a move in his ancient feud against Helena, Menele has done two things. First, he has dominated a ghoul, Roarke, into kidnapping Lodin, the Prince of Chicago. Second, he has had a letter delivered to Prince Modius of Gary, demanding the player characters present themselves to him in Chicago. The intent is that the players become scapegoats for the Prince's disappearance, and thus have to try to save him to clear their names, thus embedding themselves among the rulers of Chicago for Menele to use as pawns later, since Lodin and most of the other major players in the city belong to Helena.<br /> <br /> It's convoluted, but OK, he's an ancient vampire with psychic powers, and 'manipulation by all-knowing methuselahs' is what you expect in old-school Vampire, I can roll with all that.<br /> <br /> But here's what I'm stuck on: Where did that letter come from? It is delivered to Gary by Annabelle, Helena's grandsire, who appears to be firmly under Helena's control. It is said to be from Lodin, who is also under Helena's control.<br /> <br /> So how did Menele arrange this part? Presumably Lodin didn't actually write it, but who did? I'm less concerned with the actual writing of the letter itself, than with how it wound up with Annabelle convinced it was real, and delivering it on Lodin's behalf?<br /> <br /> Is this ever actually answered? If not I can just make something up obviously, but I figured I'd check if there is a real answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2076-mrapophenia","name":"MrApophenia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-22T02:19:06-07:00","id":1559556,"title":"","content":"While it is said to be from Lodin but that is the magician's trick<br /> Menele &quot;freed&quot; (or &quot;stole, depending how you interpret it) Annabelle from Helena and while she is her grand-Childe Helena not really cared about her and after she ate Mar\u00eda aka. her Sire &quot;disappeared&quot; and she took her place, obviously made her a bit worried even if she not knew why Mar\u00eda went off the map and I think that gave the edge to Menele to win that psychic tug-of-war<br /> Menele's goal was to strip Helena of her power base. To do this, he had to remove Lodin from the chessboard.<br /> The letter was intentionally provocative to cause chaos and spark a war between Gary and Chicago. Not to mention to Menele dragged the characters in with the letter so that they, as &quot;outsiders&quot;, would trigger events that the local vampires controlled by Helena could not calculate.<br /> So either Annabelle wrote it and been Dominated to belive she is not or one of Menele's servants or even Menele himself<br /> Either case Annabelle probably was Dominated<br /> The it could be a prelude or part of the War of Chicago if you want a deep dive in an even complicated plotline - The Temple of the Fanum/Sept of Jupiter Caern had almost thirty Garou mostly Uktena the ancient allies of Menele, and its members maintained good relations with the Gangrel of Chicago, tho' Menele was not responsible for that one, it was the Sabbat, Helena belived Menele used the big guns<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-22T06:43:43-07:00","id":1559559,"title":"","content":"Thank you! Is that info about Annabelle revealed in one of the later supplements? It doesn't appear to be in Ashes to Ashes or Chicago by Night 1E, unless I missed it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2076-mrapophenia","name":"MrApophenia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-04-22T07:07:36-07:00","id":1559561,"title":"","content":"Actually, I did find it in the Chicago by Night book! (It is not mentioned in the character sections for any of these characters, it is in 'Secrets within Secrets' on p. 22.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2076-mrapophenia","name":"MrApophenia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-02T14:08:15-07:00","id":1559704,"title":"","content":"I thought it was written by Lodin before he was kidnapped in ASHES TO ASHES.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"r